        "call": "Checker().canMeasureWater(x, y, target, {result})",
        "checker": "from math import gcd\n\nclass Checker:\n    def canMeasureWater(self, x, y, target, result):\n        if not isinstance(result, bool):\n            return False\n        if any(type(v) is not int for v in (x, y, target)):\n            return False\n        if x < 1 or y < 1 or target < 1:\n            return False\n        expected = target <= x + y and target % gcd(x, y) == 0\n        return result is expected\n"
      }
